hello_world_languages
  purpose "The top 20 languages create-test-repo.mjs picks from, each with what is needed to produce a working Hello World: the file name, how it is run, and what it must print. Data, so adding a language is a data change and never a Rust branch (ARCHITECT-VISION.md section 1)."
  programs "The program text itself lives beside this file, one per language, in examples/hello-world/<slug>/<file>. It is not embedded here because canonical Links Notation has no escape for a quote inside a quoted scalar, and every Hello World but one contains a quote. Keeping source in source files is the honest reading of that constraint rather than a workaround for it."
  source "https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/create-test-repo.mjs"
  expected_output "Hello, World!"
  verified "Each program below was written to a file and executed on 2026-09-12. Eleven printed exactly Hello, World! on this machine: python, javascript, typescript, go, rust, ruby, java, cpp, csharp, swift, fsharp. Nine had no toolchain installed locally and are unverified: kotlin, scala, haskell, elixir, clojure, ocaml, erlang, julia, r. The unverified nine are the reason the ladder runs in CI rather than only here."
  language
    name Python
    slug python
    file hello.py
    run "python3 hello.py"
  language
    name JavaScript
    slug javascript
    file hello.js
    run "node hello.js"
  language
    name TypeScript
    slug typescript
    file hello.ts
    run "npx tsx hello.ts"
  language
    name Go
    slug go
    file hello.go
    run "go run hello.go"
  language
    name Rust
    slug rust
    file hello.rs
    run "rustc hello.rs -o hello && ./hello"
  language
    name Ruby
    slug ruby
    file hello.rb
    run "ruby hello.rb"
  language
    name Java
    slug java
    file Hello.java
    run "java Hello.java"
  language
    name "C++"
    slug cpp
    file hello.cpp
    run "g++ hello.cpp -o hello && ./hello"
  language
    name "C#"
    slug csharp
    file Hello.cs
    run "dotnet script Hello.cs"
  language
    name Swift
    slug swift
    file hello.swift
    run "swift hello.swift"
  language
    name Kotlin
    slug kotlin
    file Hello.kt
    run "kotlinc Hello.kt -include-runtime -d hello.jar && java -jar hello.jar"
  language
    name Scala
    slug scala
    file Hello.scala
    run "scala Hello.scala"
  language
    name Haskell
    slug haskell
    file hello.hs
    run "runghc hello.hs"
  language
    name Elixir
    slug elixir
    file hello.exs
    run "elixir hello.exs"
  language
    name Clojure
    slug clojure
    file hello.clj
    run "clojure -M hello.clj"
  language
    name "F#"
    slug fsharp
    file hello.fsx
    run "dotnet fsi hello.fsx"
  language
    name OCaml
    slug ocaml
    file hello.ml
    run "ocaml hello.ml"
  language
    name Erlang
    slug erlang
    file hello.erl
    run "escript hello.erl"
  language
    name Julia
    slug julia
    file hello.jl
    run "julia hello.jl"
  language
    name R
    slug r
    file hello.R
    run "Rscript hello.R"
